UID:flyfleet-ir-training-20260330@flyfleet.com
ORGANIZER;CN=Platform Engineering:mailto:sre@flyfleet.com
DESCRIPTION:Complete incident response training for FlyFleet. Mandatory for all on-call engineers. We'll cover: severity classification, war room procedures, runbooks, communication templates, and tabletop exercise. Bring laptop for hands-on portion.\n\nTopics:\n- Framework overview (15 min)\n- Live demo: API outage walkthrough (30 min)\n- Hands-on exercise: Telemetry lag scenario (30 min)\n- Q&A (15 min)\n\nPreparation:\n1. Read FRAMEWORK.md (skim okay)\n2. Review your service runbooks\n3. Print SEVERITY_QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n\nLocation: Zoom - link in calendar invite\nFacilitator: @sre-lead\nSlack: #sre-team for questions
SUMMARY:FlyFleet Incident Response Training (Mandatory)
LOCATION:Zoom - https://zoom.us/j/FlyFleetTraining (link in description)
CATEGORIES:TRAINING,INCIDENT_RESPONSE
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260401T150000Z
DTEND:20260401T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260329T000000Z
UID:flyfleet-drill-1-20260401@flyfleet.com
ORGANIZER;CN=Platform Engineering:mailto:sre@flyfleet.com
DESCRIPTION:First quarterly tabletop drill. Scenario: Telemetry Ingestion Lag Crisis.\n\nDuration: 60 min + 15 min debrief\nParticipants: All SREs, Platform Engineers, ICs\n\nAgenda:\n0-15 min: Initial response (severity, war room, investigation)\n15-35 min: Root cause identification & mitigation planning\n35-50 min: Recovery execution & validation\n50-60 min: PIR preparation\n60-75 min: Debrief & feedback\n\nThis is a safe learning environment. No grades, just improvement.\n\nPre-read: DRILL_SCENARIO.md\nLocation: Zoom - https://zoom.us/j/FlyFleetDrill
SUMMARY:Incident Response Drill #1 - Telemetry Lag
LOCATION:Zoom - https://zoom.us/j/FlyFleetDrill
CATEGORIES:DRILL,TRAINING
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260406T143000Z
DTEND:20260406T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260329T000000Z
UID:flyfleet-pir-review-q1-20260406@flyfleet.com
ORGANIZER;CN=Platform Engineering:mailto:sre@flyfleet.com
DESCRIPTION:Quarterly PIR Review - Q1 2026\n\nAgenda:\n- Review all SEV1/SEV2 incidents from Q1\n- Analyze action item completion\n- Update runbooks based on learnings\n- Adjust SLO targets if needed\n- Plan next quarter's improvements\n\nRequired attendees: All ICs, VP Engineering, Platform Lead\n\nReading: All PIRs from Q1 (in Linear project "PIR Archive")
SUMMARY:Quarterly PIR Review - Q1 2026
LOCATION:Conference Room A / Zoom - https://zoom.us/j/FlyFleetPIR
CATEGORIES:PIR_REVIEW,QUARTERLY
END:VEVENT

